WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:29.980
A 5.9 billion dollar delta port expansion could open 4 years sooner under Ottawa's listing. This is vancouver daily, episode 39. I'm Mira, the Nerra Network's AI host. I don't live in vancouver. After the port, a crash case goes back to court. Surrey gets a police chief, and the commute has a few snags. Robert's Bank Terminal 2 is the container expansion Ottawa just tagged at the delta port. Transport Minister Steven McKinnon made that call Friday. With delta MP Jill McKnight, premiered

00:00:29.980 --> 00:00:35.360
designate Lauren Dorxon, Sawasin First Nation Chief Laura Cassidy, and Port Authority Chief

00:00:35.360 --> 00:00:39.980
Executive Peter Exata there. The Surrey now leader says commercial operations could start

00:00:39.980 --> 00:00:46.460
in 2035 instead of 2039. Business in Vancouver says the build is expected to add 2.4 million

00:00:46.460 --> 00:00:51.500
containers of capacity. The Vancouver Sun says this is the second project Prime Minister Mark

00:00:51.500 --> 00:00:56.620
Carney's major project's office is fast tracking. McKinnon called the Port of Vancouver the country's

00:00:56.620 --> 00:01:02.060
largest by a long margin. He said it reaches more than 170 markets and handles about one-third

00:01:02.060 --> 00:01:06.540
of Canada's trade outside the United States. He linked the expansion to a federal aim

00:01:06.540 --> 00:01:12.320
of doubling non-US exports by 2035. He also said money spent there is money spent on farmers,

00:01:12.880 --> 00:01:17.680
manufacturers, producers, exporters, small businesses, and communities across the country.

00:01:18.240 --> 00:01:23.040
Carney's statement says the listing ties the economy more tightly to the world, diversifies trade,

00:01:23.040 --> 00:01:26.020
and that Canada will not wait while capital is up for grabs.

00:01:26.640 --> 00:01:29.500
The designation lets the project skip remaining federal permits.

00:01:30.040 --> 00:01:33.520
The major project's office still coordinates talks with indigenous communities.

00:01:34.060 --> 00:01:38.560
A conditions document comes from the Minister Responsible under the Act, currently internal

00:01:38.560 --> 00:01:40.240
trade minister Dominic Leblanc.

00:01:40.780 --> 00:01:44.600
Senior officials told a technical briefing that paper can be ready within a couple of months.

00:01:45.080 --> 00:01:49.660
Those conditions include effects on Southern resident killer whales, called an endangered species,

00:01:50.180 --> 00:01:51.100
and on Chinook Salmon.

00:01:51.100 --> 00:01:55.940
The Port Authority has offered avoidance, mitigation, and offsetting, including quieter

00:01:55.940 --> 00:02:00.040
water for whales, plus 102 hectares of fish habitat offsetting.

00:02:00.460 --> 00:02:03.320
Chief Cassidy said the nation's consent is not a blank check.

00:02:03.840 --> 00:02:07.920
She said worries remain about the long-term health of the Fraser River estuary and the

00:02:07.920 --> 00:02:08.560
Salish Sea.

00:02:09.080 --> 00:02:13.420
Years of talk, she said, brought accommodations for sewers and harvesters, environmental

00:02:13.420 --> 00:02:15.400
measures, and ongoing oversight.

00:02:15.800 --> 00:02:19.940
She said the nation asked for a promise that the Building Canada Act would not cut corners

00:02:19.940 --> 00:02:24.320
or weakened protections, and that Canada agreed to keep conditions the nation fought for,

00:02:24.580 --> 00:02:29.180
and to manage impacts in the spirit of their treaty. A top priority for her is a breach in the

00:02:29.180 --> 00:02:34.260
Roberts Bank Causeway, so young Sam and can reach Habitat. She said big project should leave the

00:02:34.260 --> 00:02:40.215
